$\begin{align}
8^6\cdot 8^4&=8^{6+4}
\\\\
&=8^{10}
\end{align}$

This follows from the general rule $x^m\cdot x^n=x^{m+n}$. Note that the powers have the same base.

We can also see this is correct by expanding the powers.

$\begin{align}
8^6\cdot 8^4&=\underbrace{8\cdot 8\cdot 8\cdot 8\cdot 8\cdot 8}_\text{6 times}\cdot\underbrace{8\cdot 8\cdot 8\cdot 8}_\text{4 times}
\\\\\\
&=\underbrace{8\cdot 8\cdot 8\cdot 8\cdot 8\cdot 8\cdot 8\cdot 8\cdot 8\cdot 8}_\text{10 times}
\\\\
&=8^{10}
\end{align}$
